name unicode-case-folding
# CaseFolding.txt. The header names the fields:
#   "# <code>; <status>; <mapping>; # <name>"
#   "# T: special case for uppercase I and dotted uppercase I"
# Only the rows of status T attest here: the rows of status C, F and S are the mappings the XML gives as cf and
# scf. A row says its status and its mapping, as the text it is.
match CaseFolding.txt

tier row by \n
comment hash
remark hash
padded
names code status mapping
tier field by ;

thing row code
range code
codepoints mapping
content status
when status is T
# The header: "<code>; <status>; <mapping>; # <name>" ... "T: special case for uppercase I and dotted uppercase I ... For
# Turkic languages (tr, az), this mapping can be used instead of the normal mapping for these characters." The
# normal mapping is the XML's cf (Case_Folding); this one is the special case, worded as the header words it
relation "special case for uppercase I and dotted uppercase I" mapping
# The header: "The status field is: C: common case folding, ... F: full case folding, ... S: simple case folding, ... T:
# special case for uppercase I and dotted uppercase I": a value of the file's own list
value - status
attest row mapping status
